@ghostId = 64b7f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0

### 0. Logout first, so there is no cookie
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### U1. Me without a token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me

### U2. Me with a fake token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### U3. Me as Sara -> 200, user without password
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U4. All users as Sara (normal user) -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U5. All users as admin -> 200 with the list and a count
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U6. All users with no token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users





### U7. Sara reads her own id -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U8. Sara reads the admin's id -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U9. Admin reads Sara -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U10. Admin, an id that does not exist -> 404 "User not found"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{ghostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U11. Admin, a broken id -> 400 "Invalid value for _id"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### U12. No token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{saraId}}

### U13. Sara, an id that does not exist -> 403 (the same answer as U8)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{ghostId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### U14. Sara, a broken id -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}




### U15. Name only -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Hassan" }

### U16. Email with capitals and spaces -> 200, saved as lowercase without spaces
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  SARA.New@Example.com " }

### U17. Both fields, back to the original email -> 200 (run right after U16)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali", "email": "sara@example.com" }

### U18. Nothing to change -> 400 "Please provide name or email"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### U19. Name is an object -> 400 "name must be text"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": { "$gt": "" } }

### U20. Empty name -> 400 "Please provide name"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "" }

### U21. Short name -> 400 "Name must be at least 3 characters"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ab" }

### U22. Bad email -> 400 "Please provide a valid email"
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nope" }

### U23. Email already used by the admin -> 409 "Duplicate value entered for email..."
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com" }

### U23b. Admin's email with capitals and spaces -> 409 (the clean value is checked)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  ADMIN@Example.COM " }

### U24. Sneaking in role and password -> 200, but both are ignored
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali", "role": "admin", "password": "hacked123" }

### U25. No token -> 401
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara Ali" }